# Git commits — no Co-authored-by

When creating or amending git commits in this repo:

- **Never** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` or any similar Cursor/agent trailer.
- Commit messages must contain **only** the human-authored title and body — no bot co-author lines, no `Signed-off-by` unless the user asks.
- If amending or rewriting history to clean trailers, strip lines matching `^Co-authored-by: Cursor`.

## Commit message format

```text
Short imperative summary (≤72 chars).

Optional body: what changed and why, in complete sentences.
```

## Examples

```text
# ✅ GOOD
Fix apply_miner_fair_pool rsync to preserve VPS secrets and env files.

Exclude .env.* and .secrets/ from delete sync so remote deploy cannot wipe production configuration.

# ❌ BAD — do not append this
Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
```

Use HEREDOC for commits (`git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF' ... EOF)"`) and verify with `git log -1 --format=%B` that no `Co-authored-by` line is present before pushing.
